{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And his bow remained firmly set.</b> It was established with strength." "<b>His bow.</b> His strength." "<b>And the arms of his hands were made supple.</b> This is the giving of a ring upon his hand — a term like זָהָב מוּפָז. This came to him from the hands of the Holy One, blessed be He — He is אֲבִיר יַעֲקֹב. And from there he rose to become רֹעֶה אֶבֶן יִשְׂרָאֵל — the mainstay of Israel, a term like הָאֶבֶן הָרֹאשָׁה, a term of kingship. And Onkelos too, thus he rendered: וְתָבַת בְּהוֹן נְבִיאוּתֵהּ — the dreams that he dreamed for them; this is about maintaining the Torah in secret — it is an addition, not from the Hebrew language of Scripture. And וְשַׁוִּי תוּקְפָא רוֹחֲצָנֵהּ — that is the translation of בְּאֵיתָן קַשְׁתּוֹ. And thus the language of the Targum upon the Hebrew: וַתֵּשֶׁב נְבוּאָתוֹ — his prophecy resided — בִּשְׁבִיל שֶׁאֵיתָנוֹ שֶׁל הַקָּבָּ\"ה הָיְתָה לוֹ לְקֶשֶׁת וּלְמִבְטָח — because the might of the Holy One, blessed be He, was to him a bow and a trust; בְּכֵן יִתְרְמָא דְּהַב עַל דְּרָעוֹהִי — therefore the gold was cast upon his arms — לְכָךְ וַיָּפֹזּוּ זְרֹעֵי יָדָיו, a term of פָּז." "<b>The Stone of Israel.</b> A notarikon: אָב וּבֵן — אֲבָהָן וּבְנִין, Jacob and his sons. And our Sages interpreted: וַתֵּשֶׁב בְּאֵיתָן קַשְׁתּוֹ — about the subjugation of his desire regarding his master's wife; and it calls it קֶשֶׁת because the seed shoots forth like an arrow." "<b>And the arms of his hands were made supple.</b> Like וַיָּפוֹצוּ — that the seed went out from between the fingers of his hands." "<b>From the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob.</b> For the likeness of his father's image appeared to him, etc., as is found in Sotah (36b)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {2 "Rashi quotes Onkelos and his own Aramaic paraphrase extensively; the Aramaic is kept as written, untranslated within the comment, following Rashi's own procedure of explaining it in the surrounding Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:23.534544830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}